8. Flexbox
Flexbox is used to arrange elements in one-dimensional layouts.
It is useful for:
Navigation bars
Cards
Buttons
Horizontal layouts
Vertical layouts
Centering elements
Basic Example
<div class="container">
    <div>Box 1</div>
    <div>Box 2</div>
    <div>Box 3</div>
</div>
.container {
    display: flex;
}
The boxes will normally appear in a row.
Important Flexbox Properties
.container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
}
flex-direction
flex-direction: row;
flex-direction: column;
justify-content
Controls alignment on the main axis.
justify-content: flex-start;
justify-content: center;
justify-content: flex-end;
justify-content: space-between;
justify-content: space-around;
justify-content: space-evenly;
align-items
Controls alignment on the cross axis.
align-items: flex-start;
align-items: center;
align-items: flex-end;
Center an element
.container {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
}

